{
  "id": "aging-chain-population-cohorts-edu",
  "name": "Aging Chain (Population Cohorts)",
  "description": "A classic system dynamics structure demonstrating how populations age through cohorts over time. This aging chain model divides a population into 9 age decades, with individuals flowing from one cohort to the next as they age, while experiencing losses (mortality) from each cohort. This structure is fundamental to demographic modeling, customer lifecycle analysis, and inventory aging. Reference: Based on Beer Game model (Sterman, 2000). Source: https://systemdynamics.org/",
